Z||000001||terryk||01-21-2001||07:36 PM||||I've never heard that and I doubt they would, but some *name* companies did. <P>Other's just changed the calibrations when the coolant temp was -40 to 8 degrees or idle spark. When you compared them to stock, at least something was different, but if you knew what these area's are, it was obvious what they were doing.||||reg||5
Z||000002||mrfiero||01-21-2001||08:16 PM||||What FOCOA was/is doing is selling stock Federal chips to people.  Fieros originally sold in California came with a different PROM, so installing a Federal chip (what every other Fiero came with), would increase performance somewhat.<P>The problem was they had no conscience about selling these same chips to people who didn't need one (since their Fiero already had the Federal chip).||||reg||1
